;; Independent writing-coherence audit, 2026-08-08.
;;
;; Scope: sentence-level, new-reader audit of the abstract in draft9.tex and
;; all of intro-v2-generated.tex; lower-intensity sweep of the remaining prose
;; and titles in draft9.tex and part3-exotype-v9.tex. The prior file
;; coherence-annotations.edn was deliberately not read.
;;
;; Existing patterns were taken from all 23 entries in
;; futon3/library/writing-coherence/. This audit adds three patterns:
;;
;; :codex/insider-compression
;; A syntactically compact claim whose omitted subjects, mechanisms, or
;; referents can be reconstructed only by someone who already knows the paper.
;; Unlike ordinary technical compression, it cannot be decoded from adjacent
;; definitions. Test: can a domain-adjacent reader paraphrase it before reading
;; the section it summarizes?
;;
;; :codex/unglossed-coinage
;; A project-private word or metaphorical technical label (for example
;; "currency", "river", "ridge", "valley", or "exotype") used before a plain
;; description establishes its referent and measurable meaning. Test: could
;; two reasonable new readers assign materially different meanings to it?
;;
;; :codex/colourful-register
;; Figurative or dramatic wording where a literal statement is available and
;; would preserve the claim more precisely. The failure is not metaphor itself,
;; but metaphor carrying mechanism, scope, or result classification.

{:audit {:date "2026-08-08"
         :audience "A technically literate reader who has never seen this project"
         :priority [:abstract :introduction :titles :remaining-prose]
         :dry-intro-title "Causal State Information Governs Perturbation Spread, but Local Control Does Not Find the Coexisting Regime"}
 :annotations
 [{:id 1
   :file "holes/tech-notes/paper/draft9.tex"
   :quote "A permutation $\\sig$ of the eight displayed truth-table\npositions defines an operator $P_\\sig$ on those rules by\n$\\bit{\\sig(p)} := \\lnot\\,\\bit{p}$; the resulting family of $8! = 40{,}320$\npermutation-propagators is exactly classified."
   :pattern :writing-coherence/plain-language-thesis
   :severity :major
   :note "The second abstract sentence introduces displayed positions, an unexplained assignment convention, and the coined class name before giving a plain account of the operation. A new reader cannot yet tell what is permuted, what is negated, or what 'classified' covers."
   :suggest "We study 40,320 rule-rewriting operators. Each operator rearranges the eight outputs of a binary cellular-automaton rule and flips every output bit; we classify all operators in this finite family."}

  {:id 2
   :file "holes/tech-notes/paper/draft9.tex"
   :quote "$P_\\sig$ has a fixed rule exactly when\nevery cycle of $\\sig$ is even, an all-even permutation with $k$ cycles has $2^k$ of\nthem, and every fixed rule is balanced, with Langton activity $\\lambda = 1/2$."
   :pattern :writing-coherence/first-mention-undischarged
   :severity :moderate
   :note "The abstract uses 'balanced' and 'Langton activity' before explaining that balance means four of eight outputs are active. The theorem is legible only to a reader already carrying the paper's vocabulary."
   :suggest "An operator has an unchanged rule exactly when every permutation cycle has even length. If there are k cycles, it has 2^k unchanged rules, and each such rule has four active outputs out of eight (Langton's activity parameter lambda equals 1/2)."}

  {:id 3
   :file "holes/tech-notes/paper/draft9.tex"
   :quote "A\ncoordinate taking one value across every fixed point cannot discriminate among them,\nand a finite-size scan finds a broad crossover rather than a critical point, so the\nclassical parameter-space reading of the edge of chaos is closed off inside this\nfamily."
   :pattern :codex/insider-compression
   :severity :major
   :note "'Coordinate', 'broad crossover', 'critical point', 'parameter-space reading', and 'closed off' compress several distinct arguments into one sentence. A new reader cannot tell which coordinate is meant or what observation rejects which interpretation."
   :suggest "Because lambda equals 1/2 for every unchanged rule, it cannot distinguish their behavior. A separate finite-size scan also shows no sharpening transition over the tested range. These results provide no parameter value that identifies an edge-of-chaos transition in this operator family."}

  {:id 4
   :file "holes/tech-notes/paper/draft9.tex"
   :quote "We substitute a causal measurement---how far a single-cell perturbation\ntravels---and find it governed by how much of what the genotype reads is causally\ncurrent: cutting the phenotype-to-genotype edge roughly halves reach, a gain varying\nonly currency moves it smoothly, and constructions blind to the phenotype do not move."
   :pattern :codex/unglossed-coinage
   :severity :major
   :note "The sentence defines the outcome measure but not 'causally current', 'currency', 'gain', or what it means for constructions not to move. 'Currency' carries the central causal claim before it has a measurable definition."
   :suggest "We instead measure how far the effect of flipping one cell spreads. Reach is larger when rule updates use the current cell-state field: removing that input roughly halves reach, and gradually replacing current state information with a frozen reference reduces reach smoothly. Architectures that never read cell states remain at low reach."}

